A||||3||saleenfiero||Hypothetical Questions||||5||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||10-24-2000||12:28 PM||||In any engine mods, swaps, how much extra power would you need in an auto equipped car to equal an similarily equipped stick shift, performance (as in a straight line)? Is there a general extra percentage?  <BR>Also, Does the cat converter have any performance advantage other than emissions.  Up where I am, emissions ain't a thing so when I do the exhaust can it be taken off to any gain?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DrRodey||10-24-2000||01:20 PM||||First off, I don't think there is a straight percentage of more hp that would be needed.. it varies from car to car, tranny to tranny.  <BR>Secondly.  The Cat. provides a lot of resistance in the exhaust line, removing it will free that up and increase the speed of flow out of the engine giving you a few more ponys (maybe 10%).<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR> <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/smallfc.JPG"> <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A> ||||reg||2
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-24-2000||01:23 PM||||the cat if you delete it you'll loose 4-7lbft of tq a the wheels.(measured on (Dynojet model 748C) but you'll gain upper RPM hp. as for the auto uum there no set %age but 10-15% is close... the slush box the torque converter loose a lot of go. with the cat removed you'll have a sweeter! MEANER! sound. and it's worth the tq loss  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||10-24-2000||01:25 PM||||I'm not sure about the auto Vs. manual tranny. The manual is more efficient, but it takes a much better driver to make it go as well as the auto.<P>as far as the cat, well. anything that helps an engine breath (the flow of air threw then engine) will halp with high end horse power. a stright pipe/high flow exhaust w/ ported manifolds will help alot for HP, but it will also lower your torque. Big bore throtle bodies and port matching will also help, along with 1.6 rockers or a high lift cam and that's about as much as I know for improving breathing on the 2.8, unless you start getting into forced induction (turbo/super chargers). But you just can't get too much out of a 2.8. with out nitrous, high 14s are probrably the best you're going to get to. (not sure on that one, I'd be glad to hear if someone is running faster then that w/o nitrous). NOS is the cheapest way to get the power tho, search the archives, you'll find lots of info about exhaust, chargers, and nitrous.||||reg||1
